</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/Organic_Chemistry/Organic_Chemistry_(Morsch_et_al.)/21:_Carboxylic_Acid_Derivatives-_Nucleophilic_Acyl_Substitution_Reactions/21.06:_Chemistry_of_Esters" class="mt-section" id="section_16"><span id="Mechanism_in_Acidic_Conditions"></span><h4 class="lt-chem-36403 editable">Mechanism in Acidic Conditions</h4>

<p class="lt-chem-36403">Protonation allows the alcohol reactant to add to the ester carbonyl. Proton transfer to the ester's alkoxy group increases it ability to act as a leaving group.  Reforming the C=O carbonyl bond removes the leaving group and subsequent deprotonation by water forms the ester product.</p>

